{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"So far, I am happy; my last letter from Amsterdam will be in your hands, my dear! I sent it off early on Saturday, on which day I also saw the second, most varied part of the picture gallery—wonderful pieces among them—and further the former town hall, which Napoleon had had set up as an imperial palace. Setting aside this division of rooms and the furnishings, etc., the building (which the royal family still inhabits when they are in Amsterdam) is the most magnificent conception of a town house that a free, wealthy, art-loving citizenry could have conceived. After visiting a church famous for its colored windows and having lunch with Mr. D. Besseling, at whose place I, because he is a stricter Catholic than my Mr. van Ghert, ate fish both times, but excellent fish, I got on the diligence at 5 o’clock in the evening (on Saturday)."}}],"created":1795218832,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":189,"prompt_tokens":315,"total_tokens":504,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-P8izfxwqvIvzr1QUpyJEn1QiKJx3bG2X","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":315,"prompt_ms":535.315,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.6994126984126985,"prompt_per_second":588.4385828904476,"predicted_n":189,"predicted_ms":4430.346,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.565670212765955,"predicted_per_second":42.43460894476414}}